IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tulrca-types`
IMPORT `tulrca-periods`

-- Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (UK) — GOAL 2:
-- COLLECTIVE REDUNDANCIES (ss 188-192), and GOAL 3: PROTECTED INDUSTRIAL
-- ACTION (ss 238A-239).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1992-52.txt.

§ `Goal 2 — collective redundancies`

-- s 188(A1): "at least the threshold number of employees" or "20 or more
-- employees at one establishment", within a period of 90 days or less.
@ref s 188(A1), 195A
@export Must my employer consult about the redundancies under s 188 of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (UK)? Yes if it proposes to dismiss as redundant, within 90 days or less, at least the threshold number of employees set by regulations under s 195A, or 20 or more at one establishment. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Redundancy case`  @desc The numbers proposed to be dismissed within 90 days, in all and at my establishment, and the threshold number
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `consultation is required for` r IF
        r's `proposed dismissals in all` AT LEAST r's `threshold number`
    OR  r's `proposed dismissals at my establishment` AT LEAST 20

-- s 188(1A)(a): "100 or more employees as mentioned in subsection (A1)":
-- 100 or more proposed to be dismissed as redundant within the 90 days,
-- counted across the employer (F4, changed after the independent pass).
@ref s 188(1A)
GIVEN r IS A `Redundancy case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days of consultation needed for` r MEANS
    IF r's `proposed dismissals in all` AT LEAST 100 THEN 45 ELSE 30

-- s 188(1A): consultation must begin "at least 45 days" (or 30) "before the
-- first of the dismissals takes effect".
@ref s 188(1A)
@export The last day by which consultation had to begin under s 188(1A) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (UK): 45 days before the first dismissal takes effect where 100 or more are proposed, otherwise 30 days. NOTHING where s 188 does not apply. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Redundancy case`  @desc The numbers proposed and the day the first dismissal takes effect
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day for consultation to begin for` r MEANS
    IF `consultation is required for` r
    THEN JUST (`the day` (0 MINUS `the days of consultation needed for` r) `days after` (r's `first dismissal takes effect on`))
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 188(1A)
GIVEN r IS A `Redundancy case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `consultation began in time for` r IF
    CONSIDER `the last day for consultation to begin for` r
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST last THEN
        CONSIDER r's `consultation began on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST b  THEN b AT MOST last

-- s 189(4): "(a) begins with the date on which the first of the dismissals
-- ... takes effect, or the date of the award, whichever is the earlier, and
-- (b) is of such length as the tribunal determines ...; but shall not exceed
-- 180 days".
@ref s 189(4)
GIVEN r IS A `Redundancy case`, a IS A `Protective award`
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the protected period for` r `under` a MEANS
    `the earlier of` (r's `first dismissal takes effect on`) (a's `award made on`)

@ref s 189(4)
GIVEN a IS A `Protective award`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the length of the protected period under` a MEANS
    IF a's `days determined` GREATER THAN 180 THEN 180 ELSE a's `days determined`

@ref s 189(4)
@export The last day of the protected period of a protective award under s 189(4) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (UK): it begins with the earlier of the first dismissal and the award, and lasts for the days the tribunal determines, at most 180. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Redundancy case`  @desc The first dismissal date
      a IS A `Protective award`  @desc The award date and the days determined
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the protected period for` r `under` a MEANS
    `the day` (`the length of the protected period under` a MINUS 1) `days after` (`the first day of the protected period for` r `under` a)

-- s 190(2): "a week's pay for each week of the period; and remuneration in
-- respect of a period less than one week shall be calculated by reducing
-- proportionately the amount of a week's pay." Days excluded by ss 190(4),
-- (6) and 191 are an input.
@ref s 190(2), 191
@export The remuneration due to me under a protective award, under s 190(2) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (UK): a week's pay for each week of the protected period (at most 180 days), proportionately for part of a week, less the days for which I am not entitled under ss 190(4), (6) and 191. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN a IS A `Protective award`  @desc The days determined, a week's pay, and the days not payable
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my remuneration under` a MEANS
    IF payable GREATER THAN 0
    THEN a's `a week's pay` TIMES payable DIVIDED BY 7
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        payable MEANS `the length of the protected period under` a MINUS a's `days not payable`

-- s 189(5)(a)-(b), (5A): before the last dismissal takes effect, or "during
-- the period of three months beginning with that date", extended by s 292A.
@ref s 189(5), (5A), 292A
@export The last day to present a complaint of failure to consult, under s 189(5) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (UK): the end of the three months beginning with the day the last of the dismissals takes effect, extended for ACAS early conciliation by s 292A. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Redundancy case`  @desc The last dismissal date and any early conciliation
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for a protective award complaint for` r MEANS
    `the last day of` 3 `months beginning with` (r's `last dismissal takes effect on`) `extended by` (r's `early conciliation`)

-- s 192(2)(a), (2A): "before the end of the period of three months beginning
-- with the day (or ... the last of the days) in respect of which the
-- complaint is made of failure to pay", extended by s 292A.
@ref s 192(2), (2A), 292A
@export The last day to complain that my employer has not paid me under a protective award, under s 192(2) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (UK): the end of the three months beginning with the last day not paid for, extended for ACAS early conciliation by s 292A. NOTHING if no day is unpaid. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN a IS A `Protective award`  @desc The last unpaid day and any early conciliation
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to complain of non-payment under` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a's `last unpaid day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST d  THEN JUST (`the last day of` 3 `months beginning with` d `extended by` (a's `early conciliation for non-payment`))

§ `Goal 3 — protected industrial action`

-- s 238A(2)(a): dismissal is unfair if the reason or principal reason is
-- that the employee took protected industrial action. s 239(1): ss 108 and
-- 109 of the 1996 Act do not apply.
@ref ss 238A(1)-(2), 239(1)
@export Is my dismissal unfair because I took protected industrial action, under s 238A of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (UK)? Yes if I took action induced by an act protected by s 219 and that was the reason (or principal reason) for the dismissal; no qualifying period applies (s 239(1)). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN i IS A `Industrial action case`  @desc Whether I took protected industrial action and whether that was the reason
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my dismissal is unfair under s 238A for` i IF
        i's `I took protected industrial action`
    AND i's `that was the reason for the dismissal`

-- s 238(5): "date of dismissal" — the day the employer's notice was given,
-- if the contract was ended by notice; otherwise the effective date of
-- termination. s 239(2)(a): "before the end of the period of six months
-- beginning with the date of the complainant's dismissal". s 292A is not
-- applied to s 239(2) by this Act (F7).
@ref ss 238(5), 239(2)(a)
@export The last day to complain of unfair dismissal for taking part in industrial action, under s 239(2)(a) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (UK): the end of the six months beginning with the date of dismissal (the day the employer's notice was given, or else the effective date of termination). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN i IS A `Industrial action case`  @desc The employer's notice and the effective date of termination
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to complain of an industrial action dismissal for` i MEANS
    `the last day of the` 6 `months beginning with` dismissal
    WHERE
        dismissal MEANS
            CONSIDER i's `employer's notice given on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN i's `effective date of termination`
            WHEN JUST n  THEN n
